1
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:12,637
Lately, Yor has been coming home late.

2
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:18,268
We're not the type to stick our noses
into each other's business,

3
00:00:18,351 --> 00:00:20,186
so I haven't asked her about it…

4
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:24,315
I wonder what we're having for dinner

5
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:28,111
Father. When are we having dinner?

6
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:30,030
When Yor comes back home.

7
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:34,784
Bond. Predict what we're having
for dinner tonight.

8
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:42,000
I'm back.

9
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:47,464
She has a gloomy and sullen face,
and there are…

10
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:49,966
numerous cuts on her hand.

11
00:00:51,676 --> 00:00:52,886
Welcome home, Mother.

12
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:55,638
I'm glad to be back, Anya.

13
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:57,515
Welcome home.

14
00:00:58,349 --> 00:00:59,684
Shall we have dinner?

15
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:05,482
Oh, I'm not so hungry.
So please have dinner without me.

16
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,152
Okay…

17
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:14,407
Yor… are you…?

18
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:28,922
Mother is going to cry? Why?

19
00:01:40,683 --> 00:01:42,811
If I fail this…

20
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:47,774
I might lose both of them.

21
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,032
ORIGINAL WORK BY TATSUYA ENDO
SERIALIZED ON SHUEISHA'S SHONEN JUMP PLUS

22
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:21,284
Good work, everyone.

23
00:03:21,367 --> 00:03:22,660
Good work.

24
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:24,454
Good work.

25
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:25,663
Hey, Camilla,

26
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:27,165
want to go out for drinks?

27
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:28,917
Oh… well…

28
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,169
I'll pass.

29
00:03:31,836 --> 00:03:34,547
Hey, didn't you say
that you have a date tonight?

30
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,424
He canceled at the last minute.

31
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:44,849
Thank you!

32
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,640
Are we doing it again today?

33
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,607
But more importantly…

34
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:38,611
Are those tomatoes? They're squashed!
What are you doing, Yor?!

35
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:42,699
Hey Yor. You're working hard as always.

36
00:04:42,782 --> 00:04:43,783
Thanks for having me.

37
00:04:43,866 --> 00:04:46,953
This is all your fault!
If only you hadn't said that…

38
00:04:47,704 --> 00:04:49,122
MISSION: 16 YOR'S KITCHEN

39
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,707
THREE DAYS AGO

40
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:53,459
Huh? You want to learn how to cook?

41
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:57,505
Yes. The other day I made breakfast,
but because of that,

42
00:04:57,588 --> 00:05:00,133
my husband was in the bathroom all day!

43
00:05:00,216 --> 00:05:01,884
That's horrible.

44
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:04,554
If this continues, our marriage
will be in danger.

45
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:06,514
Which also means my job will be in danger.

46
00:05:06,597 --> 00:05:09,726
Can someone please help me
learn how to cook?

47
00:05:10,226 --> 00:05:11,352
Huh?

48
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:12,562
Well…

49
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:15,148
The housekeeper cooks for us in our house.

50
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:16,691
Go to a cooking class.

51
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:19,652
I know how to open a can!

52
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:22,030
Hey, what are you guys talking about?

53
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:26,534
Oh, I see! She's really good at cooking!

54
00:05:26,617 --> 00:05:27,660
Hey!

55
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:31,164
I'm begging you, Camilla!

56
00:05:31,247 --> 00:05:32,540
I don't want to.

57
00:05:32,623 --> 00:05:34,167
Why do I have to do it?

58
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:36,711
Oh, come on. Just teach her.

59
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:39,047
All right, let's meet at her house.

60
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,715
Hey there!

61
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:48,931
Therefore, I'm looking forward to
learning from you again today!

62
00:05:49,015 --> 00:05:50,683
This is the worst.

63
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:52,226
Don't say that.

64
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:56,147
You'll be in charge of tasting her
dishes again! That's your responsibility!

65
00:05:56,230 --> 00:06:00,109
Oh, yes, about that…
I called in one more person for that role.

66
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:05,990
Hooray! Hey, Sis!

67
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:07,200
Yuri!

68
00:06:07,283 --> 00:06:10,369
I heard that I could eat
one of your home cooked meals!

69
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:11,704
Oh boy…

70
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:14,707
This is Yor's younger brother?

71
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:16,709
He seems different from the pictures--

72
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:21,506
Thank you for having me, Camilla!
Thank you for taking care of my sister.

73
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:22,423
Sure…

74
00:06:23,174 --> 00:06:26,135
Is there some kind of a party
going on here today?

75
00:06:27,512 --> 00:06:29,931
What? Cooking lesson?

76
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:32,600
Don't tell Loid, it's a secret.

77
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:34,685
I want to improve secretly.

78
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:38,606
She's making a meal for Lotty?
I'm having mixed feelings now.

79
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:43,194
I'm thinking of making minestrone today.

80
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:46,948
I already told you that
you buy so many unnecessary things.

81
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:48,533
What will you use this for?

82
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:52,203
I'm sorry. I thought I could make it
delicious by adding lots of things in it.

83
00:06:54,664 --> 00:06:57,291
Let's start by peeling the potatoes.

84
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:58,459
All right!

85
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:01,879
How in the world does this happen
with a peeler?!

86
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:03,381
It's a pool of blood!

87
00:07:04,423 --> 00:07:06,676
This weapon is so hard to handle.

88
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:08,136
A peeler isn't a weapon.

89
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:10,221
Sis, I brought a bandage.

90
00:07:11,055 --> 00:07:12,390
I'm good with a knife.

91
00:07:14,976 --> 00:07:17,228
Like I said, you're cutting it too small!

92
00:07:17,311 --> 00:07:18,646
Just cut it normally!

93
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:20,148
You're amazing, Sis!

94
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:27,780
Hey! Why did you cut the cutting board?
That was my favorite!

95
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:29,574
I'm sorry. I'll replace it!

96
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:31,033
You're amazing, Sis.

97
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:34,871
Seriously, what's wrong with you?

98
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:37,290
How were you able to get married? Leave!

99
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:43,171
What's with this woman? She's being
rude to Sis. Should I execute her?

100
00:07:45,298 --> 00:07:48,176
Yor, you're hopeless.
You should just give up.

101
00:07:48,259 --> 00:07:50,636
You should divorce that handsome man.

102
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,013
No way…

103
00:07:52,096 --> 00:07:55,057
She brought up a good point! That's right.

104
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,184
Break up with him!

105
00:08:03,274 --> 00:08:05,276
Please, Camilla!

106
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:07,653
If Loid divorces me, then I'll be…

107
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:09,155
I'll be…

108
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:10,948
Back to worrying about getting arrested!

109
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:21,584
Hurry up and start cooking
the ingredients you chopped up.

110
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:23,961
I'll explain the seasonings after that.

111
00:08:24,045 --> 00:08:26,797
Quickly make that thing,
and get out of here.

112
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:31,594
She's actually pretty nice.
If only a little cynical.

113
00:08:32,553 --> 00:08:34,847
I think Camilla is a good person.

114
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:35,765
Hey!

115
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:41,979
Anyways, my first dish is complete.

116
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:48,236
Come on, Yuri! This is your time to shine!
Taste that dish for her!

117
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,904
Really? May I?

118
00:08:54,951 --> 00:08:56,244
Thank you for the food.

119
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:03,292
It's so delicious, Sis!

120
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:05,836
This tastes so nostalgic!

121
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,088
Oh my!

122
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:09,632
Wait, is he throwing up?
Is it good or not?

123
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:29,110
How in the world does something
turn out like this?

124
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:30,987
Did you follow my instructions?

125
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,947
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry!

126
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:35,032
Hey Sis. Can I have seconds?

127
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:38,619
Minestrone was too advanced for you.

128
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:42,331
Let's make something easier
like meatballs.

129
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:43,457
Okay!

130
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:49,505
It's delicious! It's so good that
I'm breaking out in a cold sweat!

131
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,132
As I'm enjoying this flavor,

132
00:09:51,215 --> 00:09:53,801
my childhood memories
are rushing back to me.

133
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:55,678
Wait, I'm seeing someone…

134
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:57,096
-Is it Mother?
-Stop, Yuri!

135
00:09:57,179 --> 00:09:58,556
Stop for a second!

136
00:09:59,765 --> 00:10:03,561
Oh, I see. Yor and her younger brother
grew up without parents.

137
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:07,064
You only had someone like this
eating your food,

138
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:09,525
and that's why your taste buds are dead.

139
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:11,027
Someone like this?!

140
00:10:11,902 --> 00:10:15,489
I thought everything would be fine
as long as it was nutritious.

141
00:10:15,573 --> 00:10:18,534
Yuri, I'm so glad that you
grew up healthy and well.

142
00:10:20,077 --> 00:10:23,080
Hey, don't you remember
something delicious

143
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:26,542
that your parents made for you?
Just as a reference.

144
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:31,255
Yuri, do you remember anything?

145
00:10:31,339 --> 00:10:32,798
Mom's cooking?

146
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:38,596
I vaguely remember her serving us
something that looked like stew.

147
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,473
It was so warm. I really liked it.

148
00:10:40,556 --> 00:10:43,225
Oh yes, it had a fried egg on top.

149
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:46,395
All right, let's try making that.

150
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:49,440
Try to remember what it tasted like.

151
00:10:50,066 --> 00:10:53,277
I think the base is a simple
southern stew.

152
00:10:54,862 --> 00:10:57,406
-Whoa!
-Once it boils, turn off the heat.

153
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:59,825
I think you should add ground paprika.

154
00:10:59,909 --> 00:11:00,826
Okay!

155
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,578
Make sure not to burn it.

156
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:04,872
Add the right amount of salt and pepper.

157
00:11:04,955 --> 00:11:06,332
I understand.

158
00:11:13,547 --> 00:11:16,926
You know, Yor…
something about you changed a little.

159
00:11:17,593 --> 00:11:21,347
You used to look like a robot
with a bored expression on your face.

160
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:25,351
Is that right?

161
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:30,356
-I wondered if it's because I got married.
-Huh?

162
00:11:30,439 --> 00:11:32,608
Why are you bragging?

163
00:11:32,691 --> 00:11:35,444
You probably just changed
your make-up or something.

164
00:11:35,528 --> 00:11:37,780
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

165
00:11:37,863 --> 00:11:41,158
Now, now.
Camilla, you're a lovely lady too.

166
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:42,326
Have confidence.

167
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:43,285
What…

168
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:47,206
By the way, I'm smelling something
good for the first time!

169
00:11:47,289 --> 00:11:49,375
Did you succeed in making this dish?

170
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,181
It's not bad.

171
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:09,728
It's delicious!

172
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:12,189
But I feel like there's something missing.

173
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:17,194
Yor, where's your hometown?

174
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:20,281
Around East Nielsberg.

175
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:25,369
If your family is from around that area,

176
00:12:25,453 --> 00:12:27,413
they might have added sour cream.

177
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:53,522
I'm so exhausted now.

178
00:12:57,443 --> 00:12:58,527
What is it?

179
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:02,281
Nothing. I was just thinking of
how cute you are.

180
00:13:05,159 --> 00:13:06,452
Shut up.

181
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:10,122
Wait.

182
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,043
Okay.

183
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:18,005
It seems like he's a smart dog.

184
00:13:18,088 --> 00:13:20,549
I'll start training him to be a guard dog.

185
00:13:22,384 --> 00:13:25,596
Father. Anya can't follow
the "wait" command.

186
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:27,431
I'm so hungry.

187
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:28,766
Yeah.

188
00:13:30,017 --> 00:13:32,520
I'm sorry for being late.

189
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:33,896
Welcome back, Yor.

190
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:40,819
What is that?

191
00:13:42,279 --> 00:13:43,364
Loid.

192
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:50,204
I will be making dinner tonight!

193
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:52,206
Oh no!

194
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:55,417
You were learning how to cook?

195
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,461
I'm sorry for keeping it a secret.

196
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:58,712
That's why she was late…

197
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:00,965
Is this southern stew?

198
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:04,343
Yes. My mother used to make this
for us a lot.

199
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:09,890
It's done.

200
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:12,935
The fried egg kind of lost its shape, but…

201
00:14:13,561 --> 00:14:14,645
Please enjoy!

202
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:20,442
It smells… safe.

203
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:22,486
The last supper.

204
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:29,493
-Delicious.
-It's delicious!

205
00:14:31,078 --> 00:14:32,830
Anya likes this!

206
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:34,915
It tastes very comforting.

207
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:47,553
What's wrong, Yor?

208
00:14:48,554 --> 00:14:49,638
I'm sorry.

209
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:54,143
I think I'm feeling relieved
looking at the two of you.

210
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:59,023
I thought I had to

211
00:14:59,106 --> 00:15:02,109
protect this life in order to
continue as an assassin.

212
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:05,738
But having the both of you approve of me,

213
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,574
and seeing your laughter,

214
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:13,829
just simply makes me so happy.

215
00:15:17,207 --> 00:15:19,627
This gave me a little bit of confidence,

216
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:23,339
to be the wife and mother of
the Forger family!

217
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:26,258
We'll be counting on you.

218
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:30,846
Oh, that's right! I made one more dish,
so please try that one too.

219
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:35,017
This is my original dish.

220
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:36,393
I want to eat it!

221
00:15:54,995 --> 00:15:57,915
What do you want,
calling me out to a place like this?

222
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,045
I fell in love with a woman.

223
00:16:05,047 --> 00:16:07,633
I see. Good for you. Bye.

224
00:16:07,716 --> 00:16:09,802
Wait! Listen to me!

225
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:11,845
MISSION: 16
THE GREAT ROMANCE SCHEME FOR THE INFORMANT

226
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:14,932
What? You want me to give you
a fool-proof date plan?

227
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:17,893
You're a professional in that field.

228
00:16:19,853 --> 00:16:22,064
The key is to do your best. Bye.

229
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:23,774
Wait, you heartless man!

230
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:26,360
You want me to sell your information
to the Secret Police?

231
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:32,658
I'm just kidding!
Oh yeah, you were asking me to

232
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:35,577
develop a new mini recording advice,
right?

233
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:38,372
I'll make that for free
as an exchange for helping me.

234
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:39,957
Okay?

235
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:45,087
Her name is Monica McBride.

236
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:48,132
She's an employee
at the cigar club on Fifth Street.

237
00:16:48,716 --> 00:16:51,593
She's 25 years old.
Her birthday is September 20th.

238
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:53,137
Her blood type is O.

239
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:57,641
Her height is 162 cm,
and she weighs 46 kg.

240
00:16:57,725 --> 00:17:00,686
Currently she's living together
with her mother and younger sister.

241
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:04,898
Her hobby is watching movies,
and her favorite movie is Ba Ba Berlint.

242
00:17:04,982 --> 00:17:06,900
Her childhood nickname is Moppy…

243
00:17:08,277 --> 00:17:09,903
Are you a stalker?

244
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:13,615
Stop looking so disgusted.
You do extensive research on people too!

245
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:15,367
Mine is for work.

246
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:16,577
You idiot!

247
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:19,955
It's a man's natural instinct
to want to know everything

248
00:17:20,039 --> 00:17:22,124
about a person he's really in love with!

249
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:25,294
Since you've already gathered
so much information,

250
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:27,796
can't you handle the rest on your own?

251
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,466
You idiot! Even the information department

252
00:17:30,549 --> 00:17:33,635
is separated into data collection,
and evaluation and analysis.

253
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,846
My expertise is just data collection.

254
00:17:35,929 --> 00:17:37,723
You don't have to brag about it.

255
00:17:38,307 --> 00:17:40,184
I'm begging you. I'm serious about this.

256
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:41,268
In order to see her,

257
00:17:41,351 --> 00:17:44,980
I visit her store every day to
smoke cigars even though I don't enjoy it.

258
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:48,901
Please have mercy on this humble,
scruffy four-eyes.

259
00:17:52,446 --> 00:17:55,741
I just need to analyze the information
and draft up a plan, right?

260
00:17:55,824 --> 00:17:58,619
Thank you so much, Twilight!

261
00:17:58,702 --> 00:18:00,162
I will call you President!

262
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:02,706
Shut up. Just wait for a moment.

263
00:18:06,919 --> 00:18:08,253
All right, it's done.

264
00:18:09,838 --> 00:18:12,800
I made a conversation flowchart
according to her character,

265
00:18:12,883 --> 00:18:15,302
which I speculated,
based on your information.

266
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:16,261
I see.

267
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,972
Let's say that you asked her
question number one.

268
00:18:19,056 --> 00:18:21,934
For example, her favorite food.

269
00:18:22,017 --> 00:18:25,395
I wrote down four possible answers
that we can anticipate.

270
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:26,939
I see.

271
00:18:27,022 --> 00:18:30,609
Then I wrote down the best response
you can give to each possible answer.

272
00:18:30,692 --> 00:18:32,653
From there, the conversation branches out

273
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,738
with the best response you can give

274
00:18:34,822 --> 00:18:36,657
for all the answers from A to D.

275
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:37,825
I see.

276
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:39,785
If you memorize this entire chart,

277
00:18:39,868 --> 00:18:43,080
and read the atmosphere, as you choose
your responses appropriately…

278
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:44,414
How can I do that?!

279
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:46,083
There are thousands of responses!

280
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:49,128
First of all, I don't know how to choose
responses "appropriately."

281
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:53,090
Give me a versatile scenario that will
work universally.

282
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:55,759
If such a thing existed,
life would be a lot easier for us.

283
00:18:58,637 --> 00:19:01,223
Should I disguise myself
and send you signals?

284
00:19:01,306 --> 00:19:03,142
I don't want you to hear our conversation.

285
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:07,688
Then you'll have no choice but to
practice having a conversation with her.

286
00:19:07,771 --> 00:19:11,358
What? With you as my partner?
That's so creepy.

287
00:19:12,151 --> 00:19:13,902
I'm just kidding. Please help me!

288
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:19,950
HE PUT ON A DISGUISE

289
00:19:33,547 --> 00:19:36,592
All right. I'm perfectly prepared now.

290
00:19:36,675 --> 00:19:39,678
Tomorrow I will use
this strategic art of conversation

291
00:19:39,761 --> 00:19:41,972
to challenge the battle with Monica.

292
00:19:42,931 --> 00:19:45,100
Please look forward to my report.

293
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:47,978
You don't have to report back to me.

294
00:19:48,061 --> 00:19:50,814
I'm seeing a shadow of death,
but will he be all right?

295
00:19:58,113 --> 00:19:59,364
Welcome.

296
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:03,702
Thank you for coming again, Franky.

297
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:09,917
Today… is… an… auspicious day…

298
00:20:12,502 --> 00:20:15,255
Excur-gen

299
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:19,259
Anya wants to go to
the playground obstacle course today.

300
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:20,928
That sounds like fun.

301
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:26,391
Oh, it's Scruffy.

302
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:28,685
Oh, the Forger family.

303
00:20:31,897 --> 00:20:34,233
Anya's going to
the playground obstacle course.

304
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:36,360
That sounds fun.

305
00:20:36,985 --> 00:20:38,445
Didn't you have that thing today?

306
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:41,198
Oh, the date?

307
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:43,867
Well, I was able to ask her out,

308
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:46,995
but she said that she forgot to turn off
her gas valve, so she went home.

309
00:20:47,579 --> 00:20:51,667
She said she'll come with me to watch
a movie next time. Aren't you proud of me?

310
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:54,461
I have some free time today,
so I guess I'll have some drinks.

311
00:20:57,839 --> 00:20:59,341
What is it?

312
00:21:03,762 --> 00:21:06,139
Damn it! Are looks all that matter?

313
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:10,269
Why can't you just go with me on one date?
That firm "No!" was so mean.

314
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:11,436
Sir.

315
00:21:12,020 --> 00:21:15,607
What is it? Stop talking to me.
Bring me another drink!

316
00:21:15,691 --> 00:21:17,442
Your cheapest drink!

317
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:21,780
I even promised Loid that I'd make
that device for free.

318
00:21:21,863 --> 00:21:24,533
I have no money and no girlfriend.

319
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:28,745
It's an 18-year-old Macallan on the rocks.

320
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:32,499
Huh? I didn't order this
damn expensive drink.

321
00:21:32,582 --> 00:21:33,750
I told you I'm poor.

322
00:21:34,501 --> 00:21:36,461
It's from that customer over there.

323
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:37,671
Huh?

324
00:21:40,257 --> 00:21:42,884
Hey. What a coincidence.

325
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:45,679
I felt like drinking too.

326
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:48,598
Twi… I mean, Loid.

327
00:21:52,269 --> 00:21:55,731
What happened to
the playground obstacle course?

328
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:57,566
Yor's taking care of it.

329
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:01,778
What? Did you come here to laugh at me?

330
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:05,532
Remember what you always used to say?

331
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:11,038
People like us
shouldn't become too attached to others.

332
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:15,542
Even if we can go out with them,
things won't work out.

333
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:20,839
Huh. It's not comforting to hear that
from someone who has a wife.

334
00:22:21,381 --> 00:22:23,300
My relationship is part of a mission.

335
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:24,468
Damn it.

336
00:22:24,551 --> 00:22:26,887
I'm going to get drunk today on your tab.

337
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:29,264
I'll join you.

338
00:24:07,571 --> 00:24:10,157
MISSION: 17 COMMENCE OPERATION GRIFFON/
FULLMETAL LADY/OMELETTE RICE

339
00:24:10,240 --> 00:24:11,575
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
